# shape: icon-font sheets: classes defined by `.x::before { content: "\f00c" }` (font from the `.fa` rule the same elements carry), a one- and a two-character glyph, a legacy :before, a compound with a type selector, and rules that are NOT icon definitions (three characters, long content, two classes, no pseudo-element, and empty content: a clearfix or spacer)
kinds=icon_class
@@@ file: src/icons.css
.fa { font-family: FontAwesome; }
.fa-check::before { content: "\f00c"; }
.fa-user:before { content: "\f007"; font-family: "Icons"; }
i.ok::after { content: "✓"; }
.caret::after { content: "abc"; }
.arrow::after { content: "ab"; }
.label::before { content: "Read more"; }
.fa.fa-x::before { content: "\f00d"; }
.no-pseudo { content: "x"; }
.clearfix::after { content: ""; }
.spacer::before { content: ; }
@@@ file: src/index.html
<!doctype html>
<html>
<head>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="icons.css">
</head>
<body>
<i class="fa fa-check"></i><i class="fa fa-user"></i><span class="caret"></span>
</body>
</html>
